{
  "_id": "9a88482195b83d4f",
  "name": "Monstrous Transformation",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/holy/chalice-glowing-gold.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Also at 6th level, you can cast aside common sense and use the full strength of your medicine to transform into a monster. As a bonus action on your turn, transform into a monstrous form of yourself. During this transformation, you gain the following benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your size becomes large, and your creature type becomes monstrosity.</li>\n<li>The temporary hit points you gain are doubled.</li>\n<li>Your unarmed strikes gain a bonus to attack and damage rolls equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded up).</li>\n<li>You gain the benefits of all three enhancements available to Experimental Medicine simultaneously.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>During this transformation, you cannot use creations. At the start of each of your turns, you must make an Intelligence saving throw, DC 15. On a failure, you lose control until the start of your next turn and must move towards and attack the closest creature.</p>\n<p>Once this transformation ends, you gain one level of exhaustion and cannot transform like this again until you finish a long rest.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
